{
  "id": "2026-10-09-margaret-hamilton",
  "title": "The woman who named software engineering has died at 90",
  "topic": "테크",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Margaret Hamilton, the engineer who wrote the software that put people on the Moon, has died at the age of ninety.",
    "In 1965 she became the first programmer hired for the Apollo project at MIT, and she ended up leading the team behind the onboard flight software.",
    "Her most famous moment came during the Apollo 11 landing.",
    "A faulty switch overloaded the onboard computer, and it threw an error that nobody in the room wanted to see.",
    "But Hamilton's team had built the software to rank its own tasks by priority, so it quietly shut down the background work and kept the landing running.",
    "Mission control trusted the code, and the crew touched down.",
    "She is also the person who coined the term software engineering.",
    "At the time, hardware was the serious discipline and software was an afterthought, so she picked a name that demanded the same respect.",
    "Colleagues told her it sounded like a joke.",
    "Today it is on millions of business cards.",
    "After Apollo she started two companies, both built around the same idea: catch errors before they happen rather than patch them afterward.",
    "She received the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016, and a LEGO figure of her came out the following year.",
    "Next time your build fails at two in the morning, remember that someone did this with rope memory and no stack trace — and tell me what you would ask her if you could."
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "아폴로 비행 소프트웨어를 이끈 마거릿 해밀턴이 90세로 세상을 떠났다.",
    "아폴로 11호 착륙 중 컴퓨터가 과부하로 오류를 냈지만, 그의 팀이 만든 우선순위 기반 소프트웨어가 배경 작업을 스스로 끄고 착륙을 지켜냈다.",
    "'software engineering' 이라는 말 자체를 만든 사람이고, 당시엔 농담 같다는 말을 들었다."
  ],
